  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.0.14\n- Change briefs now carry repository work location, component boundary, lineage, sibling tasks, source-backed context, build guidance, and the implemented behaviour each platform records.\n- Implemented behaviour must cite the landed source revision and state which acceptance criterion it covers. Unspecified covers:none rules become story-level product questions instead of private platform decisions; one human resolution can confirm every equivalent implementation, update the requirement, and open targeted amendments.\n- Cross-platform stories require an accepted shared contract before approval and one accepted, evidenced verification campaign covering every task before closure.\n- Test campaigns distinguish integration, verification, and validation, pin a revision, record executed checks and hashed artifacts, and require human acceptance before QA marks a change verified. Later change and feature acceptance, doctor, and reconciliation re-hash local QA evidence.\n- Dependencies gate implemented after the real dependency is non-rejected and deployed, while parallel work against agreed contracts remains possible. depends-on and supersedes cycles are refused atomically.\n- Project platforms are extensible lowercase slugs bounded by the project; requirements stay platform-neutral, components own concrete platforms, and shared remains record metadata.\n- MCP defaults to agent-only actors. The portal scopes platform choices to the selected project and exposes the expanded story-question, behaviour, campaign, evidence, and navigation workflows.",
